// The root fragment reads what the query text binds, and so do its
// normalization, the Reader's field and the `rsc` handle. An omitted field
// argument binds the field's default (`size` 64 over the root fragment's 32;
// `width` 16, the root fragment has none). A null literal for a root fragment
// argument binds the root fragment's default, as the text applies it (`height`
// 4); a component argument's null stays null (`tone`), and so does a root
// fragment argument's without a default, even where the field has one (`width`
// in `ServerRscArgumentNullQuery`). A variable is passed as
// is (`ServerRscArgumentVariableQuery`): the split operation has no defaults,
// so a variable bound to null normalizes as null, as the request sends it,
// unlike a stock `@no_inline` fragment's normalization (`PlainPicture_user`,
// unchanged).
